/*Question 3: Minimum Time Required to Rot All Oranges

We have a matrix of dimensions m × n, where each cell contains one of the following values:

0 → Empty cell
1 → Fresh orange
2 → Rotten orange

We need to determine the minimum time required for all fresh oranges to become rotten.

A rotten orange at position [i, j] can rot a fresh orange at the following adjacent positions:

[i-1, j] → Up
[i+1, j] → Down
[i, j-1] → Left
[i, j+1] → Right

Each rotten orange takes 1 unit of time to rot its adjacent fresh oranges.

If it is impossible to rot all fresh oranges, return -1.

Input
arr = {
    {2, 1, 0, 2, 1},
    {0, 0, 1, 2, 1},
    {1, 0, 0, 2, 1}
}
Output
All oranges cannot be rotten.
Explanation

At time 0:

2 1 0 2 1
0 0 1 2 1
1 0 0 2 1

At time 1:

2 2 0 2 2
0 0 2 2 2
1 0 0 2 2

At time 2:

2 2 0 2 2
0 0 2 2 2
1 0 0 2 2

The fresh orange 1 at the bottom-left corner can never be reached by any rotten orange.

Therefore, all oranges cannot be rotten, so the answer is:

-1

Expected Output:

All oranges cannot be rotten. */
fun main() {

    val arr = arrayOf(
    intArrayOf(2, 1, 0, 2, 1),
    intArrayOf(0, 0, 1, 2, 1),
    intArrayOf(1, 1, 0, 2, 1)
)
 // 	Time: O(m × n)
//		Space: O(m × n) in the worst case for the queue.
 println(orangesRotting(arr))

}
   fun orangesRotting(arr: Array<IntArray>): Int {
       val q = ArrayDeque<Pair<Int,Int>>()
       var fresh = 0 
       //put rotten oranges into queue
       for(i in arr.indices){
           for(j in arr[i].indices){
               if(arr[i][j] == 2){
                   q.addLast(Pair(i,j))
               }
               if(arr[i][j] == 1){
                   fresh++
               }
           }
       }
       var time = 0 
       
       val dire = arrayOf(
           intArrayOf(-1,0), // up
           intArrayOf(1,0), // down
           intArrayOf(0,-1), // left
           intArrayOf(0,1),  //right
       )
       
       while(q.isNotEmpty() && fresh > 0){
           val size = q.size
           //process one level  = one minute
           repeat(size){
               val (i, j) = q.removeFirst()
               for(dir in dire){
                   val ni = i + dir[0]
                   val nj = j+ dir[1]
                   
                   //check boundery
                   if(ni >= 0 && ni < arr.size && nj >= 0 && nj < arr[0].size){
                       //Fresh Orange
                       if(arr[ni][nj] == 1){
                           arr[ni][nj] = 2
                           fresh -- 
                           q.addLast(Pair(ni,nj))
                       }
                   }
               }
           }
           time++
       }
       
       return if (fresh == 0) time else -1
   }
